							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">Aiight hold up people...<br /><br />Sam and the other that commented on the lack of the other elements.&nbsp; ACTUALLY - Graf and Breakin was honored at the very first Hiphop Honors in &#039;04 - it was dope - the Rock Steady Crew was honored and did a whole set (it was dope) as well as Herc and Hollywood were honored for the DJ Element.&nbsp; They even had some life graf work during the bboy sets.&nbsp; <br /><br />Now what I think about this years show...<br /><br />I think Ice T SUCKED as a host in my opinion.&nbsp; Couldnt stop sayin how HARD he was and promoting his &quot;rap school&quot; show.&nbsp; Weak...<br /><br />The beginning started off VERY weak.&nbsp; I think the &quot;story of the beastie boys&quot; was lame, and they could have done alot better job at honoring a group of guys that made such an impact.&nbsp; HOWEVER their performance was dope.&nbsp; Seein MC Lyte mouthing the words was hella cool...And having the likes of Q-tip (diddy and fabulous I could have taken or leaven) - complete with the 80s fade and Buff glasses...he looked fresh - that was dope to hear Tip do a Beastie song...<br /><br />I LOVED seeing respected artists do covers of the honorees.&nbsp; Or seeing the candid shots of them in their seats mouthing the words.&nbsp; Like RZA mouthing every lyric to Rakims joints.&nbsp; Showed SO much respect.&nbsp; Then they showed Rakim do the same to the WU tracks.&nbsp; Made you realize that these cats are FANS too...<br /><br />Mike Epps comment about Ice Cubes PG-13 movie was hilarious.&nbsp; Erykah Badu&#039;s outfit was funky and scary but cool.&nbsp; <br /><br />I agree Eric, seeing KRS in a CM shirt would have been dope - HOWEVER, I was hella impressed he wore a ZULU shirt and was paying respect to Bam...there have been many rumors flying about bad blood between Zulu and the Temple of Hiphop - and he proved them wrong right there.&nbsp; <br /><br />MC Lyte proved that she still has it and she looked so wonderful.&nbsp; Lil Kim frightened me a bit.&nbsp; But it was dope to see her rock it again.<br /><br />K...Chris - I KNOW you were KIDDING about One Be Lo --- but I think they have ALOT of rappers/DJs/artists/etc to go through before honoring him.&nbsp; This is about honoring artists from back in the day.&nbsp; I think you were joking, just making sure you were, lol.&nbsp; <br /><br />oh...and...I am such a huge Rakim fan - did anyone catch the line in that new song he spit?&nbsp; About the new album just &quot;not meant to be&quot; with Dre?&nbsp; That was dope he called him out like that. However I must say - Rakim is such a laid back MC - its hard to watch him live. <br /><br />WU was a dope finale - however I felt they got totally cut off by Ice T promoting his teeny bopper rap school.&nbsp; Their performance was good - sucked that a few people were missing.&nbsp; Was anyone else bothered by Method Man holding the mic too close to his mouth - I couldnt understand him at all.&nbsp; The others were dope though...<br /><br />They honored some people that I had been waiting for them to honor the first 2 years - so I am glad they did that.&nbsp; </div>
