							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;"><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=117.msg1649#msg1649">Quote from: M on October 18, 2006, 09:31:12 am</a></div><div class="quote">Aiight hold up people...<br /><br />Sam and the other that commented on the lack of the other elements.&nbsp; ACTUALLY - Graf and Breakin was honored at the very first Hiphop Honors in &#039;04 - it was dope - the Rock Steady Crew was honored and did a whole set (it was dope) as well as Herc and Hollywood were honored for the DJ Element.&nbsp; They even had some life graf work during the bboy sets.&nbsp; <br /><br /></div>I remember the &#039;04 honors. Doesn&#039;t change anything. Its 2006. There are FAR more crews that have made a huge global impact on the world besides just Rocksteady Crew. You pretty much said it all with that last line. &quot;Life graf work during the bboy sets&quot;&nbsp; <img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Smileys/default/sad.gif" alt="Sad" border="0" /><br /><br />That&#039;s how they honor a very significant part of what makes hiphop what it is. Truely disappointing. Mind you I&#039;m a fan and own most of this year&#039;s inductees whole catalogue.<br /><br />They honored 2Pac &amp; Biggie before Rakim, Bambataa, MC Lyte &amp; Eazy E. <br /><br />Where&#039;s the honorees for Taki183, Ken Swift, Seen, Grandmaster Caz (who wrote Sugar Hill Gang&#039;s hits!), Kool Moe Dee/Treacherous Three. I&#039;ll stop now before I completely nerd up this whole post worse than I already have.&nbsp; <img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Smileys/default/lipsrsealed.gif" alt="Lips Sealed" border="0" /><br /><br /></div>
